+**Pass starts at** (Passes tab) sets where each level starts:
+
+- **Auto** cuts the rings from the middle of the area outward. This is
+  the order that 2D Offset always cut.
+- **Outside** starts at the outer edge of the area and works in. With an
+  Outside containment, the outer edge is the stock edge: the tool starts
+  outside the stock, cuts one stepover at a time and ends on the part
+  wall. Use it to stop full-width slots in the stock.
+- **Inside** starts at the part or island wall and works out.
+
 **Do not touch** (Geometry tab, **Boundaries**): pick faces or edge chains
 to protect from every cut, plunge, ramp, helix, keep-down and rapid link
 across the full tool assembly (flutes, shank and holder). **Clearance**

From f94dfa7591eacaf7dfead0137bf54a44a07fd0a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:05:30 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(2d): Pass starts at (Auto/Inside/Outside) for 2D
 Pocket

2D Pocket had no choice of where each level of rings starts. With an
Outside containment, the ring strategies cut the band core-first, so
the first ring was a full slot in the stock (the #3316 defect, on the
pocket kind).

Give OpParams::Pocket the shared #3316 field pass_start: the same type,
project key (auto never written), Passes-tab row, MCP edit_operation
door and digest bytes (only off Auto). The generator calls
pocket_started, which is pocket_entered_with_relief byte for byte on
Auto, so every golden stays the same. Waterline and Offset rings read
the value through the #3316 ring law. Zigzag rows and rest machining
have no ring order: with Inside or Outside they say so by name in the
path notes.

Pinned by pocket_pass_start (fig8.step, EM-0800-4FL, Outside
containment), pass_start_moves_the_pocket_stamp_only_off_auto and the
UI the_pocket_passes_tab_offers_pass_start_and_shows_the_draft.

Stacked on #3353.

Fixes #3354
Refs #3316
Refs #1448

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
